{
  "quest.63911AFF147BA1FD.title": "&eUtilitarian",
  "quest.5FA54ADB7A454E2D.title": "&aPig Power",
  "quest.5A811E99C409699F.title": "&3Furnace Factory",
  "task.27AF0228A67846F4.title": "Any Elevator",
  "quest.41392AB326D113C1.title": "&eNeoSync",
  "quest.766ED9C3C575F83D.title": "&aFired Up",
  "task.3583C42F09BAD32B.title": "Crafting Table on a Stick",
  "quest.4EA93D8996CBCC6F.title": "&aAngel Block",
  "quest.5CAF581D02976AD3.quest_desc": [
    "Let lightning strike &cGrrass&r and it turns into &cCursed Grrass&r, which spawns extra mobs. Neither grass has a recipe, so a storm is the only way to get it.",
    "",
    "Look at a block of it to complete the quest. A trident with Channeling can call the lightning down during a thunderstorm.",
  ],
  "quest.348DD697A85D7D46.quest_desc": [
    "&aCompressed Bone Meal&r applies 4 bone meals in one use. On a fully grown crop it harvests the crop and replants it for you.",
    "",
    "&3Extremely Compressed Bone Meal&r applies 16 and turns saplings into large fancy trees. &2Florist's Bone Meal&r spawns up to 5 flowers within 3 blocks on grass.",
  ],
  "quest.78E9F521E6662D31.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Rainbow Furnace&r produces 50,000 FE/t, but only while one furnace of each tier is running as an active generator and none of them has a full buffer.",
    "",
    "It only pushes energy out of sides set to output, and you can only have one of them.",
  ],
  "quest.5E261FCD7A5628D4.title": "&aAugments",
  "quest.77F457502E8EC957.title": "&aElevators",
  "quest.28035DF778F7D517.quest_desc": [
    "A drone's abilities come from the blocks it's built from.",
    "",
    "- &aDrill&r: on the front, the drone flies to the block you're mining and helps break it.",
    "- &2Dispenser&r: facing forward, it shoots arrows at nearby enemies without using any.",
    "- &aCactus&r: on the front, it attacks hostile mobs. A Magma Block works the same way.",
    "- &2Lodestone&r: collects nearby items and brings them to you.",
    "- &aBeacon&r: on the front, it fires a laser at enemies.",
    "- &2Light&r: any bright light block makes the drone light up the area around it.",
  ],
  "quest.5E261FCD7A5628D4.quest_desc": [
    "Augments change how a furnace behaves. Right-click one onto a furnace to insert it.",
    "",
    "- &aSpeed&r: halves the cook time but burns twice the fuel.",
    "- &2Fuel Efficiency&r: fuel heats twice as much, but cooking is 25% slower.",
    "- &aBlasting&r: limits the furnace to blasting recipes.",
    "- &2Smoking&r: limits it to smoking recipes.",
  ],
  "quest.5CAF581D02976AD3.title": "&cCursed Grrass",
  "quest.5FA54ADB7A454E2D.quest_desc": [
    "The &aTreadmill&r powers the constructor. It's two blocks long and places like a bed. Put it next to the constructor and lure an animal onto the front block.",
    "",
    "A pig makes 16 FE/t, a wolf 22, a villager 25, a creeper 80 and an enderman 160. JEI lists every animal it accepts.",
    "",
    "Any other FE source works too. A shell takes 102,400 FE to build in this pack.",
  ],
  "quest.348DD697A85D7D46.title": "&aCompressed Bone Meal",
  "quest.28035DF778F7D517.title": "&aDrone Abilities",
  "quest.26EADD4D46542B01.title": "&eModular Drones",
  "quest.4ED6DB305986636C.quest_desc": [
    "A finished shell waits in a &aShell Storage&r. Give it a redstone signal or FE and its doors open. Walk in to pick a shell and move your mind into it.",
    "",
    "Your old body stays behind with everything it carried, and each shell keeps its own inventory and experience.",
    "",
    "Dying in a shell sends you straight into another finished one. Dying in your original body is a normal death. The storage drains 16 FE/t, and if it loses power the shell inside dies 20 ticks later.",
  ],
  "quest.766ED9C3C575F83D.quest_desc": [
    "The &aGenerator&r augment turns a furnace into a power source. Heat from burning fuel becomes FE, and the furnace can no longer smelt while it's fitted.",
    "",
    "It can't be crafted in this pack, so look for it in a &2Furnace Pouch&r. &6The Gambler&r sells those for 35 coins in manors and marble chateaus, and each one holds a single random furnace item.",
    "",
    "Output depends on the tier. An &2Iron Furnace&r makes 40 FE/t and a &6Netherite Furnace&r makes 1,000 FE/t. With a &2Blasting&r augment fitted as well, it burns gems and metal ingots for a fixed amount of power each, listed in JEI under Generator | Blasting.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: &6The Gambler&r only sells once you've opened a loot crate of your own.",
  ],
  "quest.63911AFF147BA1FD.quest_desc": [
    "&eUtilitarian&r is a pile of small fixes and handy blocks. Plenty of it works without you doing anything, like sleeping with monsters nearby, leaves that decay fast after you chop a tree and farmland you can't trample.",
    "",
    "&aSnad&r is the first thing worth crafting. Sugar cane and cactus planted on it grow 3 blocks taller and get 5 extra growth ticks.",
  ],
  "quest.76429142123E3A8D.title": "&aAngry Dirt",
  "quest.54FE9DA77DED738D.title": "&fUtilities",
  "quest.4EA93D8996CBCC6F.quest_desc": [
    "The &aAngel Block&r can be placed in mid-air with nothing next to it. It's the easiest way to start a sky bridge or a floating platform, and you build off it like any other block.",
  ],
  "quest.26EADD4D46542B01.quest_desc": [
    "&eModular Drones&r lets you build a personal drone out of ordinary blocks. Place the &aDrone Assembly Controller&r, lay a platform of &2Assembly Frames&r next to it and build your drone on top.",
    "",
    "Press Build in the controller and the whole thing shrinks into a pocket drone. Wear it in the drone slot and it follows you around with no fuel needed. A drone can use up to 1,000 blocks, and heavier ones fly slower.",
    "",
    "&cRemember where the controller sat next to the frame.&r Taking a drone apart later only works with the controller back in that same spot.",
  ],
  "quest.509D7878283EC7AF.title": "&3Ion Thruster",
  "quest.78E9F521E6662D31.title": "&6Rainbow Furnace",
  "quest.66BB02961DF43CB7.quest_desc": [
    "The &aFluid Hopper&r works like a hopper for fluids, taking a step every 10 ticks.",
    "",
    "It's a cheap way to empty a machine's output tank into a tank below it without laying any pipe.",
  ],
  "quest.76429142123E3A8D.quest_desc": [
    "&aDrit&r deals 2 damage to anything standing on it, which makes it a simple floor for a mob farm.",
    "",
    "Grass can spread onto Drit, and when it does it becomes &cGrrass&r, which hurts too.",
  ],
  "quest.5A811E99C409699F.quest_desc": [
    "A &3Factory&r augment turns a furnace into a multi-slot factory that runs on power instead of fuel. It can work on up to six stacks at once, with more slots opening on higher tier furnaces.",
    "",
    "Its energy buffer holds 80,000 FE on Iron and Copper furnaces, 200,000 on Golden and Silver, and 1,000,000 on everything above that.",
  ],
  "quest.1A829C51143D3EDA.title": "&aLift",
  "quest.509D7878283EC7AF.quest_desc": [
    "The &3Ion Thruster&r is the strongest lift you can build. A big drone with a lot of blocks needs several of them to keep pace with you.",
  ],
  "quest.4EB87209B1EB584E.title": "&dZero Point",
  "quest.3FA19D4AC45FB458.quest_desc": [
    "Every furnace from &eIron Furnaces&r cooks faster than the vanilla one. The tooltip shows each furnace's cook time, and the &6Netherite Furnace&r gets it down to 5 ticks per item.",
    "",
    "You don't need to break a furnace to improve it. Hold an upgrade kit and Sneak + Right-click a placed furnace to move it up a tier without emptying it.",
  ],
  "quest.21252D2D8461718A.title": "&aNo Soliciting",
  "quest.41392AB326D113C1.quest_desc": [
    "&eNeoSync&r grows spare bodies. Build a shell, keep it in storage, and when you die in one body you wake up in the next.",
    "",
    "Place the &aShell Constructor&r with a free block above it, then right-click it with an empty hand to give it a genetic sample.",
    "",
    "&cThe sample costs 20 health, which is a full health bar, and it will kill you.&r Eat a golden apple or hold a Totem of Undying first. If you do die, the shell still starts building.",
  ],
  "quest.2C1F53BD5651CE4B.title": "&aTurning Up the Heat",
  "quest.2202B2620A3F90D7.quest_desc": [
    "A &aCrafting Table on a Stick&r is a crafting table you carry. Put it in its Curios slot, then press the Open Crafting on a Stick keybind to pick a station from a selection wheel.",
    "",
    "Items left in the grid stay there when you close it. There are stick versions of the stonecutter, smithing table, anvil, loom, grindstone and cartography table too.",
  ],
  "quest.4EB87209B1EB584E.quest_desc": [
    "The &dZero Point&r versions need no power at all. The storage keeps its shell forever and the constructor finishes a shell instantly.",
    "",
    "Taking a sample still costs the same health, so keep a golden apple handy.",
  ],
  "quest.77F457502E8EC957.quest_desc": [
    "Put two &aElevators&r in the same column and you can travel between them. Jump on one to go up to the next, or sneak to go down. They reach 384 blocks and don't need to match colors.",
    "",
    "Right-click one with a block to disguise it as that block. Right-click it with an empty hand to open its options menu.",
  ],
  "quest.2C1F53BD5651CE4B.quest_desc": [
    "Keeping every furnace stocked with coal gets old, so &eIron Furnaces&r lets you heat them with power instead.",
    "",
    "Make a &aWireless Heat Transmitter&r and give it FE. Then make a &aWireless Heat Receiver&r and place it inside that block to bind the two, and any furnace with the Receiver in its fuel slot runs off the stored power.",
    "",
    "Each charge pulls 2,000 FE from a buffer of 1,000,000 FE and lasts one smelt, or two with a &2Fuel Efficiency&r augment. The Receiver is never used up, and it only works in Iron tier furnaces and up.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: Both items share one name in your inventory. The one you can place is the &aWireless Heat Transmitter&r, and its tooltip tells you to link it.",
  ],
  "quest.3FA19D4AC45FB458.title": "&eIron Furnaces",
  "quest.4ED6DB305986636C.title": "&aSpare Body",
  "quest.0B239918FC4D92ED.quest_desc": [
    "The &aPersonal Shrinking Device&r can change the player size when charged.",
    "",
    "Right-click to access its interface and Shift + Right-click to shrink or expand.",
  ],
  "quest.2202B2620A3F90D7.title": "&aCrafting on a Stick",
  "quest.54FE9DA77DED738D.quest_desc": [
    "This chapter collects the small mods that make daily life easier. None of them is a progression line of its own, so pick up whatever helps.",
    "",
    "The furnaces are on the right, &eUtilitarian&r is on the left, &eNeoSync&r is below and &eModular Drones&r is above. The four quests on the corners are single tools you can grab at any time.",
  ],
  "quest.66BB02961DF43CB7.title": "&aFluid Hopper",
  "quest.21252D2D8461718A.quest_desc": [
    "Wandering traders love to turn up in the middle of your base. A &aNo Soliciting Banner&r keeps them away within 6 chunks.",
    "",
    "If you want the traders without the clutter, a &aSoliciting Carpet&r makes arriving traders appear on the carpet instead. The trapped version kills them on arrival.",
  ],
  "quest.1A829C51143D3EDA.quest_desc": [
    "A drone needs rotors to fly. The &aWooden Rotor&r gives 10 thrust, the &2Advanced Rotor&r 25 and the &3Ion Thruster&r 40.",
    "",
    "&cA rotor with any drone block one or two blocks below it gives no thrust.&r Keep the space under your rotors clear.",
  ],
}